# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo (release DOIs).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use accelrun, please cite it using these metadata."
title: accelrun
version: 0.1.0
# keep date-released in sync with the actual v0.1.0 tag date
date-released: "2026-11-05"
authors:
  - family-names: Terrosi
    given-names: Francesco
type: software
license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FrancescoTerrosi/accelrun"
abstract: >-
  Zero-dependency launcher that attaches host accelerators (NVIDIA, AMD,
  Apple Metal, custom, CPU) to Docker containers as vendor-neutral
  resources: raw device nodes + bind-mounted driver libraries, no NVIDIA
  Container Toolkit, any Docker version. Workloads consume an abstract
  accelerator resource via the ACCEL_* environment contract, with optional
  vendor-neutral CDI publication.
keywords:
  - gpu
  - containers
  - docker
  - cdi
  - accelerator
  - unified-memory
